menu "Test"

config TEST
	bool "Build selftests (tools/testing/selftests)"
	default y
	help
	  Build the kernel-style selftests under tools/testing/selftests for un
	  and, in place, for the crypto and hpc submodules, so `make check` can
	  run them from object tree. Covers the cmocka unit tests and the
	  perf benchmarks. The Catch2 (C++) unit suite and net-dependent bats are
	  wired separately and gated on their own prerequisites.

	  If unsure, say Y.

config BENCHMARK
	bool "Performance benchmarks"
	default n
	help
	  Build and run the performance benchmarks under
	  tools/testing/selftests/perf/ during `make check`

	  If unsure, say N.


config CMOCKA
	bool "Enable cmocka unit test framework"
	depends on CC_CLIB
	default y
	help
	  Enable building cmocka-based unit tests. When enabled,
	  'make check' will build and run all cmocka test suites.

	  cmocka requires libc support (CONFIG_CC_CLIB=y).

	  If unsure, say Y.

config CMOCKA_TAP
	bool "Use TAP output format for cmocka"
	depends on CMOCKA
	default y
	help
	  Output test results in Test Anything Protocol (TAP) format
	  for easy integration with CI/CD systems.

	  If unsure, say Y.

config CHECK_SUBMODULES
	bool "Run submodule tests during make check"
	depends on CMOCKA
	default y
	help
	  When enabled, 'make check' will also discover and run
	  tests defined in submodules (e.g., vendor/hpc/tests).

	  If unsure, say Y.

endmenu
